        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most buyers the <strong class="text-white">Horizon 7.0 AT</strong> is the one to buy: a
            60-inch deck, 15% incline, open app support, three years of parts cover and a lifetime
            frame and motor warranty at a sale price around $1,000. Regular runners should step up
            to the <strong class="text-white">7.4 AT</strong> for the wider deck and five years of
            parts cover.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Walkers on a budget should look at the <strong class="text-white">T202</strong>, and the
            heaviest users at the <strong class="text-white">7.8 AT</strong>. Whichever you choose,
            buy at the sale price, check the ship date, and accept that you will set the incline
            yourself — that is the price of never paying a subscription.
          </p>
